This function uses a modified merge sort algorithm to efficiently count inversions. The idea is to split the array into halves, recursively sort them, and then count the inversions while merging the sorted halves. The key step is that whenever an element in the right half is placed before an element in the left half, it indicates the presence of inversions. The number of inversions found in this step is `(mid - i + 1)`

